{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app","sessionId":"6f6ea2e5-a897-4eee-b071-f5d83e4defb2","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"a2dd1b7","slug":"lovely-hatching-hollerith","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"I need to understand the format of this instance.txt file for a job-shop scheduling problem. The file content is:\n\n```\n4 3\n3\n2 0 6 1 5\n2 1 7 2 6\n2 0 5 2 8\n3\n2 0 5 2 7\n2 1 6 2 5\n2 0 7 1 8\n3\n2 1 4 2 6\n2 0 8 1 7\n2 0 6 2 5\n3\n2 0 7 1 6\n2 1 5 2 7\n2 0 4 2 6\n```\n\nLine 1 says \"4 3\" meaning 4 jobs, 3 machines (machines 0, 1, 2).\nThen for each job, there's a line with the number of operations (3 in all cases), followed by that many operation lines.\n\nEach operation line appears to start with the number of machine options, then pairs of (machine, duration).\n\nFor example, for Job 0, Operation 0: \"2 0 6 1 5\" means 2 options: machine 0 with duration 6, or machine 1 with duration 5.\n\nThis is a flexible job-shop scheduling problem (FJSP) where each operation can be processed on different machines with different processing times.\n\nPlease confirm this interpretation. Also note that lines with just \"3\" indicate number of operations for the next job.\n\nResearch if there's a standard format for FJSP instance files and verify this interpretation."},"uuid":"5ba8ddab-dcec-46c9-8f06-5245c9c1b159","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:56:27.111Z"}
